<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<!--
  Who may carry a razor.

  Canonically a razor is forbidden to every Color but Gold, and merely touching
  one is punishable by death. Vanilla cannot express that: Precept_Weapon gates by
  weapon CLASS, not by who is holding it, and there is no history event raised for
  equipping a weapon at all. So the enforcement lives in
  Source/RimRising/HarmonyPatches.cs, and this file is the belief it enforces.

  IT IS A LAW, NOT A LAW OF PHYSICS. The restriction only binds pawns whose
  ideoligion actually holds the precept. A raider, a resistance fighter, or a
  colony that never adopted the hierarchy can pick up a razor freely - and the
  Society's fury about that is the entire point. The Rising began, in part, with
  lowColors being handed razors precisely because of what it meant.

  Issue structure mirrored from Ideology/Defs/PreceptDefs/Precepts_Weapons.xml.
-->
<Defs>

  <IssueDef>
    <defName>RR_RazorBearing</defName>
    <label>razor bearing</label>
    <iconPath>UI/Issues/RR_RazorBearing</iconPath>
  </IssueDef>

  <!--
    Raised when someone the hierarchy considers unfit takes up a razor anyway.
    Fired from the Harmony patch, since vanilla raises nothing on equip.
  -->
  <HistoryEventDef>
    <defName>RR_LowColorBoreRazor</defName>
    <label>a lesser Color bore a razor</label>
  </HistoryEventDef>

  <!-- =============================== the Society ========================== -->

  <PreceptDef>
    <defName>RR_RazorBearing_GoldOnly</defName>
    <issue>RR_RazorBearing</issue>
    <label>Gold alone</label>
    <description>The razor is the proof of the right to rule, and it is not a thing to be held by hands that were made for other work. A lesser Color who takes one up has not committed theft. They have committed a claim.</description>
    <impact>High</impact>
    <displayOrderInIssue>10</displayOrderInIssue>
    <associatedMemes>
      <li>RR_ColorHierarchy</li>
    </associatedMemes>
    <conflictingMemes>
      <li>RR_ColorEquality</li>
    </conflictingMemes>
    <comps>
      <li Class="PreceptComp_UnwillingToDo">
        <eventDef>RR_LowColorBoreRazor</eventDef>
        <description>Bear a razor while not of Gold</description>
      </li>
      <li Class="PreceptComp_KnowsMemoryThought">
        <eventDef>RR_LowColorBoreRazor</eventDef>
        <thought>RR_KnowLowColorBoreRazor</thought>
        <description>Someone unworthy bore a razor</description>
      </li>
    </comps>
  </PreceptDef>

  <!-- ============================= the resistance ========================= -->

  <PreceptDef>
    <defName>RR_RazorBearing_Anyone</defName>
    <issue>RR_RazorBearing</issue>
    <label>any hand</label>
    <description>They told us for eight hundred years that the blade knows whose hand it is in. It does not. It is a meter of wire and a switch, and it cuts for anyone.\n\nSo let it be seen being carried.</description>
    <impact>Medium</impact>
    <displayOrderInIssue>20</displayOrderInIssue>
    <associatedMemes>
      <li>RR_ColorEquality</li>
    </associatedMemes>
    <conflictingMemes>
      <li>RR_ColorHierarchy</li>
    </conflictingMemes>
    <comps>
      <li Class="PreceptComp_KnowsMemoryThought">
        <eventDef>RR_LowColorBoreRazor</eventDef>
        <thought>RR_KnowLowColorBoreRazor_Approved</thought>
        <description>One of ours bore a razor</description>
      </li>
    </comps>
  </PreceptDef>

  <!-- ================================ thoughts ============================ -->

  <ThoughtDef>
    <defName>RR_KnowLowColorBoreRazor</defName>
    <thoughtClass>Thought_Memory</thoughtClass>
    <durationDays>12</durationDays>
    <stackLimit>5</stackLimit>
    <stages>
      <li>
        <label>a lesser Color bore a razor</label>
        <description>Someone who had no right to it carried a razor. It is not the blade that offends. It is what carrying it says.</description>
        <baseMoodEffect>-8</baseMoodEffect>
      </li>
    </stages>
  </ThoughtDef>

  <ThoughtDef>
    <defName>RR_KnowLowColorBoreRazor_Approved</defName>
    <thoughtClass>Thought_Memory</thoughtClass>
    <durationDays>12</durationDays>
    <stackLimit>5</stackLimit>
    <stages>
      <li>
        <label>one of ours bore a razor</label>
        <description>One of us carried a razor openly, where it could be seen. Eight centuries of being told that was impossible, and it turns out it only ever required doing it.</description>
        <baseMoodEffect>6</baseMoodEffect>
      </li>
    </stages>
  </ThoughtDef>

</Defs>
